  "problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y={log}_{8}⁡x?$\n\nI. The domain is $x\\ge 0$\n\nII. It has no horizontal asymptotes\n\nIII. It passes through the point $(64,2)$",
  "worked_solution": "Let's plot the graph of $y={log}_{8}⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14245974/assets/6811e57f1259b97448811ac9abe8d6fc7f76a52b62e685f2fa0ec36e290381b4.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. From the graph, we see that the domain is $x>0.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, the function $y={log}_{8}⁡x$ has no horizontal asymptote. However, it does have the vertical asymptote $x=0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Substituting $x=64$ into the equation of the curve gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={log}_{8}⁡(64) \\\\  & ={log}_{8}⁡({8}^{2}) \\\\  & =2{log}_{8}⁡(8) \\\\  & =2\\,\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn conclusion, only statements II and III are true.",
